-4.46,"twoYearChangeBp":-5,"slopeChangeBp":-5},{"speechDate":"2024-08-28","controlDate":"2024-09-04","controlBefore":"2024-09-03","controlAfter":"2024-09-05","nearChangeBp":-3.21,"deferredChangeBp":-16.95,"twoYearChangeBp":-13,"slopeChangeBp":2},{"speechDate":"2024-09-20","controlDate":"2024-10-25","controlBefore":"2024-10-24","controlAfter":"2024-10-28","nearChangeBp":0.99,"deferredChangeBp":9.03,"twoYearChangeBp":5,"slopeChangeBp":2},{"speechDate":"2024-10-23","controlDate":"2024-10-16","controlBefore":"2024-10-15","controlAfter":"2024-10-17","nearChangeBp":4.99,"deferredChangeBp":3.0,"twoYearChangeBp":1,"slopeChangeBp":5},{"speechDate":"2025-01-06","controlDate":"2024-12-30","controlBefore":"2024-12-27","controlAfter":"2024-12-31","nearChangeBp":-0.98,"deferredChangeBp":-6.55,"twoYearChangeBp":-6,"slopeChangeBp":2},{"speechDate":"2025-01-31","controlDate":"2025-01-24","controlBefore":"2025-01-23","controlAfter":"2025-01-27","nearChangeBp":-2.48,"deferredChangeBp":-11.52,"twoYearChangeBp":-12,"slopeChangeBp":0},{"speechDate":"2025-02-25","controlDate":"2025-03-04","controlBefore":"2025-03-03","controlAfter":"2025-03-05","nearChangeBp":0.83,"deferredChangeBp":-0.96,"twoYearChangeBp":3,"slopeChangeBp":9},{"speechDate":"2025-06-26","controlDate":"2025-07-24","controlBefore":"2025-07-23","controlAfter":"2025-07-25","nearChangeBp":-0.48,"deferredChangeBp":6.01,"twoYearChangeBp":3,"slopeChangeBp":-3},{"speechDate":"2025-07-22","controlDate":"2025-08-05","controlBefore":"2025-08-04","controlAfter":"2025-08-06","nearChangeBp":0.03,"deferredChangeBp":1.05,"twoYearChangeBp":0,"slopeChangeBp":0},{"speechDate":"2025-08-09","controlDate":"2025-08-16","controlBefore":"2025-08-15","controlAfter":"2025-08-18","nearChangeBp":0.74,"deferredChangeBp":1.5,"twoYearChangeBp":2,"slopeChangeBp":-1},{"speechDate":"2025-08-22","controlDate":"2025-08-15","controlBefore":"2025-08-14","controlAfter":"2025-08-18","nearChangeBp":3.75,"deferredChangeBp":5.49,"twoYearChangeBp":3,"slopeChangeBp":2},{"speechDate":"2025-08-28","controlDate":"2025-08-14","controlBefore":"2025-08-13","controlAfter":"2025-08-15","nearChangeBp":7.01,"deferredChangeBp":10.5,"twoYearChangeBp":8,"slopeChangeBp":1},{"speechDate":"2025-11-03","controlDate":"2025-12-08","controlBefore":"2025-12-05","controlAfter":"2025-12-09","nearChangeBp":0.28,"deferredChangeBp":6.01,"twoYearChangeBp":5,"slopeChangeBp":-1},{"speechDate":"2025-11-11","controlDate":"2025-11-25","controlBefore":"2025-11-24","controlAfter":"2025-11-26","nearChangeBp":-0.53,"deferredChangeBp":-0.5,"twoYearChangeBp":-1,"slopeChangeBp":-3}],"method":"For each CPI/jobs-screened speech in date order, search one through six weeks away on the same weekday, checking the earlier date first at each distance. Require identical two contract reference dates and bracket length, both Treasury marks, and no Board, FOMC, CPI or Employment Situation date in the inclusive comparison bracket. Never reuse a comparison quote bracket. Match eligibility and date without using the sign or size of the moves. Paired excess equals the absolute speech-bracket move minus the absolute comparison-bracket move, then the median across pairs. Other economic releases remain possible on either date."},"methods":["Start with every communication in the Federal Reserve Board speech index during the Atlanta tracker observation span through the last complete year, including Chair, Vice Chairs and governors. Exclude one written essay as an event, while retaining it for overlap detection. Reserve Bank presidents and Congressional testimony indexed elsewhere fall outside this list.","Using only the last strictly earlier tracker observation, choose the earliest future or current-day quarterly reference start and a reference start 260–290 days farther out. Each of the two fixed contracts must have a mean at all three marks. Earlier change spans the fifth-to-last through last strictly earlier observation (four intervals). Across-speech change runs from the last strictly earlier to the first strictly later tracker date. The maximum spans are 12 and seven calendar days respectively. No event-day quote is used.","The Atlanta Fed recovers option-implied three-month average SOFR means from CME options. Levels and changes are in basis points. A move in these quarterly means can reflect expected policy and risk premia. It does not measure the probability or size of the next FOMC decision.","Treasury 2-year and 10-year par yields use the same two endpoint dates. 2s10s means the 10-year yield minus the 2-year yield. Treasury observations and option inputs have no synchronized intraday timestamp here. Quotes cover market developments before and after the speech.","Screen the inclusive quote bracket for any other Board index entry or FOMC decision, conference or minutes date. Releases, economic news, testimony and Reserve Bank speeches may still overlap. A sensitivity check also excludes the inclusive bracket around BLS Consumer Price Index and Employment Situation releases using the publication dates on archived editions. The four-interval pretrend is context and has no overlap screen. Adjacent brackets can share a price observation, so event counts are descriptive.","Every retained date gets equal weight. Quartiles use linear interpolation on sorted observations. Suppress sign comparisons for jointly small moves by requiring both absolute moves to exceed 1 bp. The Chair subgroup is descriptive. Independently reviewed text scores, when available, are joined by speech URL and event date. Missing text scores remain empty."],"sources":[{"label":"Federal Reserve Board speech index","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/speeches.htm"},{"label":"Board speech-index data","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/json/ne-speeches.json"},{"label":"Atlanta Fed Market Probability Tracker","url":"https://www.atlantafed.org/en/research-and-data/data/market-probability-tracker"},{"label":"Historical option distributions (XLSX)","url":"https://www.atlantafed.org/-/media/Project/Atlanta/FRBA/Documents/research-and-data/data/market-probability-tracker/mpt_histdata.xlsx"},{"label":"US Treasury daily par yield curve","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?type=daily_treasury_yield_curve"},{"label":"Federal Reserve monetary policy calendars and minutes","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm"},{"label":"BLS Employment Situation archived releases","url":"https://www.bls.gov/bls/news-release/empsit.htm"},{"label":"BLS Consumer Price Index archived releases","url":"https://www.bls.gov/bls/news-release/cpi.htm"},{"label":"SF Fed US Monetary Policy Event-Study Database","url":"https://www.frbsf.org/research-and-insights/data-and-indicators/us-monetary-policy-event-study-database/"}],"events":[{"date":"2023-04-18","title":"Considerations for a Central Bank Digital Currency","speaker":"Governor Michelle W. Bowman","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/speech/bowman20230418a.htm","isChair":false,"priorStart":"2023-04-11","beforeDate":"2023-04-17","afterDate":"2023-04-19","nearReferenceStart":"2023-06-21","deferredReferenceStart":"2024-03-20","nearPriorBp":10.48,"nearMeanBeforeBp":507.94,"nearChangeBp":3.53,"deferredPriorBp":16.46,"deferredMeanBeforeBp":405.46,"deferredChangeBp":10.91,"twoYearChangeBp":6,"slopeChangeBp":-6,"textScore":null,"blsReleaseInBracket":""},{"date":"2023-05-05","title":"Commencement Address","speaker":"Governor Lisa D. Cook","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/speech/cook20230505a.htm","isChair":false,"priorStart":"2023-04-28","beforeDate":"2023-05-04","afterDate":"2023-05-08","nearReferenceStart":"2023-06-21","deferredReferenceStart":"2024-03-20","nearPriorBp":-12.49,"nearMeanBeforeBp":496.0,"nearChangeBp":10.99,"deferredPriorBp":-48.52,"deferredMeanBeforeBp":346.5,"deferredChangeBp":34.51,"twoYearChangeBp":25,"slopeChangeBp":-10,"textScore":null,"blsReleaseInBracket":"2023-05-05 Employment